          "text": "{\"regions\":{\"r2\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"ploughs. \u0905\u0930\u094d\u0915\u092e\u0942\u0932\u0938\u094d\u092f\u2014The root of the Arka ( calatropis Gigantia;\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"\u0930\u0941\u0908 in Mar\u00e1thi ) is a worthless plant. Cf. the proverb \u0905\u0930\u094d\u0915\u0947 \u091a\u0947\u0928\u094d\u092e\u0927\u0941\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":4,\"text\":\"\u0935\u093f\u0928\u094d\u0926\u0947\u0924 \u0915\u093f\u092e\u0930\u094d\u0925\u0902 \u092a\u0930\u094d\u0935\u0924\u0902 \u0935\u094d\u0930\u091c\u0947\u0924\u094d \u0964 \u0915\u0930\u094d\u092a\u0942\u0930\u0916\u0923\u094d\u0921\u093e\u0928\u094d\u2014( \u0916\u0923\u094d\u0921 m =a collection )\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":5,\"text\":\"a collection of karpura plants. \u0935\u0943\u0924\u094d\u0924\u093f\u0902\u2014from \u0935\u0943 to cover, to\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":6,\"text\":\"surround+\u0924\u093f ( \u0915\u094d\u0924\u093f\u0928\u094d ) what surrounds, a hedge. \u0915\u094b\u0926\u094d\u0930\u0935\u093e\u0923\u093e\u092e\u094d\u2014\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":7,\"text\":\"\u0915\u094b\u0926\u094d\u0930\u0935 is a kind of very poor and coarse grain, and is commonly\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":8,\"text\":\"known as \u0939\u0930\u0940\u0915 \u0915\u0930\u094d\u092e\u092d\u0942\u092e\u093f\u2014lit. the land of religious rites i. e.\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":9,\"text\":\"\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":10,\"text\":\"this world as opposed to \u092d\u094b\u0917\u092d\u0942\u092e\u093f ( such as Swarga, the world\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":11,\"text\":\"of the moon &c. ). \u2018The idea is somewhat similar to that of\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":12,\"text\":\"Bishop Butler who calls this a world for man\u2019s probatin.\u2019\u2014\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":13,\"text\":\"Telang. Hindu writers refer by this to India ( the land of\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":14,\"text\":\"Bharata \u092d\u0930\u0924\u0935\u0930\u094d\u0937 ) which is the fittest land for the performance\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":15,\"text\":\"of religious rites. It is laid down in S\u2019ruti ( see Chh\u00e1nd. Up. )\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":16,\"text\":\"that men repair to the world of the moon &c. to reap the bene-\",\"end\":\"hyphen\"},{\"n\":17,\"text\":\"fits of their meritorious deeds; and when the fund of happiness\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":18,\"text\":\"laid in store there for them is exhausted they come down again\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":19,\"text\":\"to this world of mortals to perform karman. Cf. \u0915\u0930\u094d\u092e\u092d\u0942\u092e\u093f\u092d\u0942\u0924\u0947\u093d-\",\"end\":\"hyphen\"},{\"n\":20,\"text\":\"\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":21,\"text\":\"\u0938\u094d\u092e\u093f\u0928\u094d \u092d\u093e\u0930\u0924\u0947 \u0935\u0930\u094d\u0937\u0947 \u0964 Kad. p 457. \u0915\u0930\u094d\u092e\u092d\u0942\u092e\u093f\u092e\u093f\u092e\u093e\u0902 \u092a\u094d\u0930\u093e\u092a\u094d\u092f \u0915\u0930\u094d\u0924\u0935\u094d\u092f\u0902 \u0915\u0930\u094d\u092e \u092f\u091a\u094d\u091b\u0941\u092d\u092e\u094d\u2019 \u0964\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":22,\"text\":\"\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":23,\"text\":\"R\u00e1m\u00e1. Ayod. K. \u0915\u0930\u094d\u092e\u092d\u0942\u092e\u093f\u0930\u093f\u092f\u0902 \u092c\u094d\u0930\u0939\u094d\u092e\u0928\u094d \u092b\u0932\u092d\u0942\u092e\u093f\u0930\u0938\u094c \u092e\u0924\u093e \u0964 quoted by\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":24,\"text\":\"\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":25,\"text\":\"Mr. Telang from Muir. V. 324. \u0924\u092a\u0938\u094d\u2014is used here in a wider\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":26,\"text\":\"sense; as meaning the performance of one\u2019s religious duties\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":27,\"text\":\"of all sorts, necessary to elevate one to heaven. The idea ex-\",\"end\":\"hyphen\"},{\"n\":28,\"text\":\"pressed here is this. Men, who waste the opportunity of securing\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":29,\"text\":\"heaven ( or moksha\u2019 ) by practising tapas, given to them by\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":30,\"text\":\"birth in this world, are as foolish as one who &c. The fig. is\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":31,\"text\":\"\u092e\u093e\u0932\u093e\u0928\u093f\u0926\u0930\u094d\u0936\u0928\u093e.\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":true,\"note\":\"Several Sanskrit readings and the printed spelling \u2018prob atin\u2019 are unclear in the scan.\"},\"r3\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"Sl. 107 The moral Mr. Telang draws from this verse is \u201cA\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"man may do the most difficult and dangerous things in order\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"to do what is fated not to happen, or to avoid what is fated to\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":4,\"text\":\"happen. But he will fail.\u201d There is no reference in this verse,\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":5,\"text\":\"however, to \u201c avoiding what is fated to happen.\u201d The verse\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":6,\"text\":\"says that although a man may dive into the sea ( for pearls or\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":7,\"text\":\"other gems), go to the golden mountain, Meru, conquer enemies\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":8,\"text\":\"in battle, or carry on trade and so forth, no wealth comes to\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":false,\"note\":null},\"r1\":{\"type\":\"page_number\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"( 41 )\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":false,\"note\":null}},\"units\":[{\"id\":\"u1\",\"type\":\"notes\",\"number\":null,\"label\":null,\"open_start\":true,\"open_end\":true,\"children\":[\"u2\",\"u3\"]},{\"id\":\"u2\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":null,\"label\":null,\"open_start\":true,\"open_end\":false,\"children\":[\"r2\"]},{\"id\":\"u3\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":\"107\",\"label\":null,\"open_start\":false,\"open_end\":true,\"children\":[\"r3\"]}],\"flows\":[{\"flow\":\"main\",\"units\":[\"u1\"]}],\"relations\":[]}"
        }
